    <item>
      <title>From: Bill, To: Bess Chandler</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1911/07/02/547/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 02 Jul 1911 23:56:06 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1911/07/02/547/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17570054_0180.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140501_17570054_0180&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17570054_0180.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17570935_0181.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140501_17570935_0181&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/postcard-2014-20140501_17570935_0181.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Bill, To: Bess Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Louisiana, Missouri on July 2, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Bessie Chandler&lt;br&gt;
503 N. School St,&lt;br&gt;
Normal, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hello Bess,&lt;br&gt;
Why don’t you write? This is two I have written. I am home on a visit, my brother is here. How are you standing this weather? Answer soon.&lt;br&gt;
Bill&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>From: Bill, To: Ruby Chandler</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/1911/06/21/1290/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Jun 1911 18:09:10 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/1911/06/21/1290/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140613_12110868_0564&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140613_12110868_05641.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140613_12111597_0565&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/postcard-2014-20140613_12111597_0565.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;br&gt;
From: Bill, To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Wichita, Kansas on June 21, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Miss Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
253 N. Estelle Ave.&lt;br&gt;
Wichita, Kansas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;June 21 second time up. Only month one and the bees have been making love to the trees for quite a while . When are you coming home. Be sure and get here by the eighth, to take a ride in Bessie’s auto. Don’t let Wichita take up with you.&lt;br&gt;
Bill&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
